From 6495360dc13e1373309a26a14058060fcb33e1ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:54:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] android: move the app's sources to the Tangelo package

The Android app's Kotlin sources still lived in Citra's package, org.citra.citra_emu, while
the application ID was already io.github.microworldwide.tangelo. Move them to
io.github.microworldwide.tangelo (folder, package lines, Gradle namespace, navigation and
layout XML, proguard rules) and rename everything the native code ties to it: the JNI
function names (Java_org_citra_citra_1emu_... -> Java_io_github_microworldwide_tangelo_...,
also in the setting-keys template) and the class names passed to FindClass/GetMethodID,
including one signature string that was split over two lines.

Checked: no old name left (also with adjacent string literals joined), every Kotlin file's
package matches its folder, and every external fun has its JNI function (137 setting keys
from the template, run() in its overloaded form).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
